    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s matchup today, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) represent our most potent offensive engines. **Butler** benefits significantly from the matchup against Javier; the high expected ERA of 5.16 creates an elite environment for his dynamic platoon edge (+13%). Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in a prime spot against Nick Martinez, where favorable park factors and a strong 17% SP skill boost push him to near-elite efficiency levels. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) remains a core start as well, with his 16% park boost against Baz anchoring his high daily floor. We are leaning heavily into these positive matchup environments to maximize our runs and RBI potential while maintaining our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.\n\nThe decision to start **Justin Crawford** (57.03) over **Jung Hoo Lee** (50.65) was the most difficult pivot of the day. While **Jung Hoo Lee** provided a reasonable score, his efficiency was capped by a negative dynamic platoon adjustment against the left-handed Bennett. **Justin Crawford** remains in the lineup due to his aggressive base-running upside, which aligns with our team mandate to prioritize speed in a scarcity-driven format. We are keeping a close eye on **Cal Raleigh** (55.95), who faces the toughest assignment of the day against the formidable Imanaga. His score is bolstered by a +6% dynamic platoon advantage, but the 3.69 xERA of the opposing starter introduces enough risk that he sits at the lower end of our starting confidence interval. There are no immediate weather threats reported, but with several hitters facing mid-tier arms like Javier and Martinez, we expect significant production throughout the heart of the order.",
